title: moon1_cassian_first_meet_echohaven
---
Cassian: *(emerging from the south path, hands raised in a friendly gesture)*
Cassian: Hello there. You must be the one Milo's been talking about.
Cassian: Cassian. I study the old architectures. I heard your hum from three valleys over.
Cassian: Magnificent work on the dome.
===

title: moon1_cassian_about_milo
---
Cassian: Milo is a Tartarian fox spirit — a *foxikit*, in the old tongue. They were the first guides.
Cassian: He sees more than he says. Listen when he goes quiet.
===

title: moon1_cassian_warning_resets
---
Cassian: There are others who want this work undone, you understand.
Cassian: Reset agents. They believe the cycle should be allowed to complete. They believe the world wants to forget.
Cassian: I disagree, of course. That is why I came to find you.
===

title: moon1_cassian_about_song
---
Cassian: The song is real. The hum is real. *Frequency* is real.
Cassian: The Tartarians knew that matter is just standing waves. So they sang to it. And it stood up.
Cassian: When you tune a node, you are not playing music. You are *building*.
===

title: moon1_cassian_farewell_echohaven
---
Cassian: I should walk on. There are other valleys to find.
Cassian: We will meet again — at the Lunar Moon, perhaps, or the Bronze.
Cassian: Be careful what you trust, traveler. Be careful who you sing for.
===
